    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d940">

                <pb facs="1012" n="1002" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1002"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6363/2–1149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Cabot</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-11T18:00:00-05:00">February 11,
                            1949—6 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>260. As tentatively indicated in exploratory discussions (Deptel 2282, Dec
                        30<anchor n="9" xml:id="d940-f1"/>) oil cos have been informed Dept agreed
                    desirable if cos were to limit petroleum stock Shanghai not exceed supply 6
                    weeks bulk, 6 months packaged goods. Cooperation British Emb requested with view
                    concurrent action Shell.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
